<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Opava</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Troppau</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Opava (German: Troppau) is a city in the Moravian-Silesian Region of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czech-republic">Czech Republic</a>, on the Opava river. It was the seat of the Duchy of Opava, ruled by a branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/premyslid-dynasty">Přemyslid dynasty</a>, and from 1742 the capital of Austrian Silesia. In 1820 it hosted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-troppau">Congress of Troppau</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-alliance">Holy Alliance</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/opava.jpg" alt="Opava" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MOs810 · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Horn%C3%AD_n%C3%A1m%C4%9Bst%C3%AD,_Opawa,_Opava-M%C4%9Bsto_(1).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
